From 1aa1b1d9536d2b0bf29f29d97f45a2772d848152 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Beany <24502088+beanyforever@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:30:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] A restored page reads with its restored attributes

Restoring a page from its history (RollbackDocHistory, behind
/api/history/rollbackDocHistory) or one page from a snapshot
(RollbackRepoSnapshotFile, behind /api/repo/rollbackRepoSnapshotFile)
rewrites the page's file and reindexes it, and the write caches the page's
copy and its page attributes, but neither drops its blocks' cached
attributes. So /api/attr/getBlockAttrs kept serving the attributes from
before the restore, custom-object-type and custom-avs among them, until
SiYuan restarted, while the file and SQL held the restored ones. A block
deleted since the version restored came back with the attributes it had when
deleted, since deleting a block drops none of its cached attributes; and a
block the restore removed kept what an edit had cached under its bare id,
where getBlockAttrs looks for a block the block index no longer lists.

Both now drop, once the page is written, the cached attributes of every
block of the page, as deleting a page does: the blocks it held before the
restore, as the block index listed them, and those of the restored version.
A block fill that read the page before the write is already refused by the
write, as 0004 has it, so what is read next comes from the restored file.

Their Go tests are in restore_cache_fts5_test.go.
TestRollbackDocHistoryRestoresAttributes takes a page's history, then
changes the page's custom-object-type, changes its paragraph's custom-shelf
and deletes the paragraph, adds a blockquote with a custom-shelf of its own
and edits the paragraph in it; it restores the page and reads all three
through getBlockAttrs. TestRollbackRepoSnapshotFileRestoresAttributes does
the same with a snapshot and a repository key. Without the patch, on v3.8.7
with 0001 to 0006 applied, both read the page's and the paragraph's changed
values and the removed blockquote's, though the file holds the restored
version; without the drop of the blocks held before, the blockquote's, and
without the drop of the restored version's, the paragraph's. Under the race
detector the history test, like SiYuan's own history restore tests, reports
the fixture's cleanup setting Conf back while RollbackDocHistory's own
goroutine reads it.

Still open: SiYuan's command-line restores, history rollback and repo
rollback, run in their own process, so they still leave the kernel's caches
as they were, as its command-line move does.
